{{!--
    The paper doll. Two grids: the body around the portrait, and the weapons in
    a row of thirds beneath it.

    Every slot is the same markup whether it is empty, filled or broken — the
    state is classes and content, not three branches, because a drop target that
    changes shape as it fills is a drop target that moves under the cursor.
--}}
<div class="squire-build">


    {{!-- The rail: every build this character has, and the only place they are
          managed. It replaced a section in the tray, which spent a lot of a
          narrow column on something touched rarely — and split one feature in
          two, since editing happened here and applying happened there.

          Entries drag onto the tray handle, which is how a build gets somewhere
          reachable with the tray shut. --}}
    <div class="squire-build-rail">

        {{!-- Which kinds of entry the list shows. Blacksmith's own tab bar, so
              the shape, the states and the accent are the suite's rather than
              this window's; the only thing set here is the track, because three
              tabs have 170px of rail to share and the primitive is built for a
              full-width window.

              Words, and no icons. The three labels only just fit across the rail
              and an icon beside each would push them onto a second line — and of
              the two, the word is the half that says which is which. The count
              rides in the tooltip for the same reason. --}}
        <nav class="blacksmith-tabs squire-build-rail-tabs">
            {{#each railTabs}}
            <button type="button" class="blacksmith-tab squire-build-rail-tab{{#if this.active}} is-active{{/if}}"
                    data-filter="{{this.key}}"
                    data-tooltip="{{this.count}} {{#if (eq this.count 1)}}entry{{else}}entries{{/if}}">
                {{this.label}}
            </button>
            {{/each}}
        </nav>

        <div class="squire-build-rail-list">
            {{#each rail}}
            {{!-- A tile, not a row.

                  Its face is what most distinguishes this entry from the one
                  above it: for a costume its own picture, which is the whole of
                  what a costume is; for a build the character's headline choice,
                  the spell a caster leads with or the weapon anybody else does.

                  The marks under it are the portrait and the token — what
                  wearing this would make you LOOK like, which is the one thing
                  the doll does not show. A weapon thumbnail used to sit among
                  them and appeared on costumes too: switching a build to a
                  costume leaves its gear slots filled on purpose, so that
                  switching back restores them, and the tile was reading that
                  slot without asking what kind of thing it was drawing. --}}
            <div class="squire-build-rail-entry{{#if this.active}} is-active{{/if}}"
                 draggable="true" data-build-id="{{this.id}}"
                 style="background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(8,6,4,.55), rgba(8,6,4,.88)), url('{{this.tileImage}}');"
                 data-tooltip="{{this.name}}<br><em>Drag onto the tray handle to keep it to hand</em><br><em>Right-click for more</em>">
                <div class="squire-build-rail-text">
                    <div class="squire-build-rail-head">
                        <span class="squire-build-rail-name">{{this.name}}</span>
                        {{!-- Blacksmith's own primary-button class carries the
                              colour, so the green here is the green every other
                              action button in the suite uses and cannot drift
                              from it. Squire only overrides the SHAPE. --}}
                        <button type="button" class="squire-build-rail-apply blacksmith-window-btn-primary"
                                data-build-id="{{this.id}}"
                                data-tooltip="{{#if this.costume}}Wear this costume{{else}}Equip this build{{/if}}">
                            {{!-- The icon says which of the two this tile is, and
                                  matches the button that made it: the masks on
                                  the New Costume button, the shirt on the
                                  launcher that opens builds at all. --}}
                            <i class="fa-solid {{#if this.costume}}fa-masks-theater{{else}}fa-shirt{{/if}}"></i>
                        </button>
                    </div>

                    {{!-- Directly under the name, where a subtitle goes: what
                          this entry IS, in the fewest marks that say it. --}}
                    <div class="squire-build-rail-stats">
                        {{#unless this.costume}}
                        <span data-tooltip="Estimated armour class"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield"></i> {{this.armorClass}}</span>
                        <span data-tooltip="Items in this build"><i class="fa-solid fa-shirt"></i> {{this.gearCount}}</span>
                        {{else}}
                        <span><i class="fa-solid fa-masks-theater"></i> Costume</span>
                        {{/unless}}
                    </div>

                    {{#if this.isDefault}}
                    {{!-- The character's DEFAULT ARTWORK came from this entry:
                          what they look like when nothing says otherwise, which
                          is what a build with no image of its own falls back to
                          and what the next token placed will be stamped with.

                          A third kind of fact again. Selected is what this window
                          shows, worn is what they have on, and this is what they
                          look like underneath both — so it sits above the worn
                          line, since it outlasts it.

                          It is a SNAPSHOT, so it can go stale: editing this
                          costume's pictures afterwards leaves the default
                          describing something this no longer looks like. Said
                          rather than hidden, with the same warning triangle the
                          worn mark uses for the same situation. --}}
                    <div class="squire-build-rail-default{{#if this.defaultDrifted}} is-drifted{{/if}}"
                         data-tooltip="{{#if this.defaultDrifted}}New builds start from this entry's artwork, and its pictures have changed since.<br><em>Set it as the default again to catch up</em>{{else}}What a new build or costume starts from in this tool. The character is not affected{{/if}}">
                        {{#if this.defaultDrifted}}
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> Default (changed)
                        {{else}}
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-user-circle"></i> Default
                        {{/if}}
                    </div>
                    {{/if}}

                    {{#if this.worn}}
                    {{!-- Its own line under the counts, because it is a different
                          KIND of fact from them. Selected is what this window is
                          showing; WORN is what the character actually has on, and
                          the rail is the only place both are visible at once.

                          LAST WORN is the third fact: still the plan in play, and
                          the character has since parted company with it. Not
                          "modified", which claimed something the check cannot
                          see — the plan and the character disagree, and nothing
                          here knows which of the two moved. --}}
                    <div class="squire-build-rail-worn{{#if this.drifted}} is-drifted{{/if}}"
                         data-tooltip="{{#if this.drifted}}The last build applied, but the character no longer matches it &mdash; {{this.driftCount}} difference{{#unless (eq this.driftCount 1)}}s{{/unless}}.<br><em>Equip it again to put it back</em>{{else}}This is what the character is currently wearing{{/if}}">
                        {{#if this.drifted}}
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> Last worn
                        {{else}}
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i> Worn
                        {{/if}}
                    </div>
                    {{/if}}
                </div>

                {{!-- On the hem, and as wide as the tile allows. They are the
                      answer to "what would I look like", which wants to be
                      looked at rather than glanced past at 26px. --}}
                <div class="squire-build-rail-preview">
                    {{#if this.portrait}}<img src="{{this.portrait}}" alt="Portrait" data-image-kind="portrait" data-tooltip="Portrait">{{/if}}
                    {{#if this.token}}<img src="{{this.token}}" alt="Token" data-image-kind="token" data-tooltip="Token">{{/if}}
                </div>
            </div>
            {{/each}}

            {{!-- The tab is on and has nothing to show. Said out loud, because a
                  blank strip looks like a window that failed to load rather than
                  like a filter doing its job. --}}
            {{#if railFiltered}}
            <div class="squire-build-rail-none">No {{railFilterLabel}} yet</div>
            {{/if}}
        </div>

        {{!-- Two buttons, not one and a switch. You know which of the two you
              are setting out to make before you start; the switch beside the
              name is for changing your mind afterwards. --}}
        <div class="squire-build-rail-actions">
            <button type="button" class="squire-build-rail-new" data-mode="gear"
                    data-tooltip="A set of gear to equip">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-shirt"></i> Build
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="squire-build-rail-new" data-mode="costume"
                    data-tooltip="A portrait and token to wear. Changes how the character LOOKS and touches no gear.">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-masks-theater"></i> Costume
            </button>
        </div>

        {{!-- Options that belong to BUILDS, not to any one build. The rail is
              where they go for the same reason the list is: it is the part of
              this window that is about the whole feature rather than the thing
              currently on the doll. --}}
        <div class="squire-build-rail-global">
            <div class="squire-build-rail-global-label">Options</div>
            <div class="blacksmith-toggle-row squire-build-rail-option"
                 data-tooltip="Equipping a build also puts its Main Hand, Both Hands and Off Hand weapons on the tray handle, replacing whatever the last build put there. Items you dragged onto the handle yourself are never touched.">
                <span class="blacksmith-toggle-label">Weapons on handle</span>
                <label class="blacksmith-toggle">
                    <input type="checkbox" class="blacksmith-toggle-input squire-build-handle-input"
                           {{#if updatesHandle}}checked{{/if}}>
                    <span class="blacksmith-toggle-slider"></span>
                </label>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="squire-build-workspace">
    {{#if build}}
    {{!-- ONE grid for the whole workspace, in both modes and for both kinds of
          character. The title is a row of it rather than a band above it, so it
          stops where the doll stops and the rule beside it runs the full height
          the way the rail's does. Its second row is pinned to the doll's height,
          which is what makes a costume and a build the same size — and what
          stops toggling between them resizing the window. --}}
    <div class="squire-build-columns{{#if isCaster}}{{#unless isCostume}} has-pack{{/unless}}{{/if}}">

    <div class="squire-build-title-row">
        {{!-- The name reads as a heading and edits as a field. It was a
              full-width boxed input, which made the least important thing in the
              window the biggest — it only needs to be reachable, not
              announced. --}}
        <input type="text" class="squire-build-name" value="{{build.name}}"
               maxlength="60" spellcheck="false" aria-label="Build name">

        {{#unless isCostume}}
        {{!-- Fill this build from what the character is wearing NOW. The answer
              to having set a kit up on the sheet before finding this window, and
              to the commoner case of changing something there and wanting the
              build to catch up. --}}
        <button type="button" class="squire-build-pull"
                data-tooltip="Fill from currently equipped &mdash; takes what the character is wearing now into this build">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-download"></i>
        </button>
        {{/unless}}

        {{#if canPrepare}}{{#unless isCostume}}
        {{!-- Prepared spells in or out, per build.

              OFF by default, and that is the point: gear and preparation are two
              decisions on two rhythms, and a build that silently unprepared a
              caster's whole list because it was written before they picked one
              is this module overreaching. Off, the column is not drawn and
              applying does not touch a single spell. --}}
        <div class="blacksmith-toggle-row squire-build-prep"
             data-tooltip="<strong>On</strong> &mdash; this build plans prepared spells, and equipping it prepares them and unprepares the rest.<br><strong>Off</strong> &mdash; it plans gear only and leaves the character's prepared list exactly as it is.">
            <span class="blacksmith-toggle-label">Prep</span>
            <label class="blacksmith-toggle">
                <input type="checkbox" class="blacksmith-toggle-input squire-build-prep-input"
                       {{#if includesPrepared}}checked{{/if}}>
                <span class="blacksmith-toggle-slider"></span>
            </label>
        </div>
        {{/unless}}{{/if}}
    </div>

    {{#if isCaster}}{{#unless isCostume}}
    {{!-- The rule between the doll and the column, mirroring the one between the
          rail and the workspace. Its own track rather than a border on either
          side: a border would eat into whichever column carried it, and the
          whole layout rests on those two being exact multiples of each other.
          It spans both rows, so it runs past the title to the top.

          Not in costume mode: there is no second column there to divide, and a
          rule with nothing on the far side of it is just a line. --}}
    <div class="squire-build-divider"></div>

    {{!-- The column's heading, in the header row beside the build's name rather
          than inside the column: above the cells it would push every one of them
          half a row out of line with the doll, which is the one thing this
          column is built not to do. Names both halves of what is under it — the
          nine ranks you can cast with, and the list you cast from. --}}
    <div class="squire-build-pack-title">Preparation</div>
    {{/unless}}{{/if}}

    {{#if isCostume}}
    {{!-- A costume is three pictures and a name. The doll is not hidden here so
          much as absent: a costume never touches gear or spells, so sixteen
          slots that can only sit empty would be a promise the mode does not
          make — and the plates, the armour class and the spell column all
          describe equipment this view has nothing to do with. --}}
    <div class="squire-build-costume">
        {{!-- The two images this costume WRITES, side by side at the top, and the
              costume's own picture filling everything under them.

              They were stacked around the picture, one above and one below, and
              that spent the column's height on three rows so all three had to be
              small. Together on one row they cost a single row between them and
              the square below gets the rest. --}}
        <div class="squire-build-costume-pair">
            {{#with portraitSlot}}
            <div class="squire-build-costume-image">
                <div class="squire-build-slot is-round squire-build-image-slot{{#unless this.isDefault}} is-set{{/unless}}"
                     data-image="{{this.key}}"
                     data-tooltip="{{#if this.isDefault}}This costume does not change the {{this.label}} — wearing it leaves the character's own alone<br><em>Click to choose an image</em>{{else}}Wearing this costume sets the {{this.label}}<br><em>Click to change, right-click to reset</em>{{/if}}">
                    {{#if this.path}}
                    <img class="squire-build-slot-image" src="{{this.path}}" alt="{{this.label}}" data-image-kind="{{this.key}}">
                    {{/if}}
                    <i class="fa-solid {{this.icon}} squire-build-slot-hint"></i>
                    {{#unless this.isDefault}}
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-dot squire-build-image-change"
                       data-tooltip="<strong>On.</strong> Wearing this sets the character's {{this.label}}.<br>Right-click the picture to switch it off, and the character keeps their own."></i>
                    {{/unless}}
                </div>
                <span class="squire-build-costume-label">{{this.label}}</span>
            </div>
            {{/with}}
            {{#with tokenSlot}}
            <div class="squire-build-costume-image">
                <div class="squire-build-slot is-round squire-build-image-slot{{#unless this.isDefault}} is-set{{/unless}}"
                     data-image="{{this.key}}"
                     data-tooltip="{{#if this.isDefault}}This costume does not change the {{this.label}} — wearing it leaves the character's own alone<br><em>Click to choose an image</em>{{else}}Wearing this costume sets the {{this.label}}<br><em>Click to change, right-click to reset</em>{{/if}}">
                    {{#if this.path}}
                    <img class="squire-build-slot-image" src="{{this.path}}" alt="{{this.label}}" data-image-kind="{{this.key}}">
                    {{/if}}
                    <i class="fa-solid {{this.icon}} squire-build-slot-hint"></i>
                    {{#unless this.isDefault}}
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-dot squire-build-image-change"
                       data-tooltip="<strong>On.</strong> Wearing this sets the character's {{this.label}}.<br>Right-click the picture to switch it off, and the character keeps their own."></i>
                    {{/unless}}
                </div>
                <span class="squire-build-costume-label">{{this.label}}</span>
            </div>
            {{/with}}
        </div>

        <div class="squire-build-token-settings">
            {{!-- All three on one row: they are one decision. How big the token
                  is, how the picture is fitted into that, and how large it is
                  drawn inside the fit — you set them together or not at all, and
                  stacked they read as three unrelated settings.

                  A control is marked ONLY when it will change something. The
                  earlier version marked the opposite — every untouched control
                  wore a "no change" tag, which put three warnings on the
                  commonest state and none on the one worth noticing. --}}
            <div class="squire-build-token-row">
                {{!-- Each field is as wide as the control in it, not a third of
                      the row: two single-digit boxes and a dropdown whose
                      longest entry is "Full Height" were both stretched across a
                      third and read as fields expecting a sentence. The scale
                      takes what is left, since a slider is the one control here
                      that is genuinely better long.

                      The mark after each caption says the control is ON — this
                      costume sets that thing. It was a caution triangle, which
                      was wrong twice over: nothing here is an error, and the
                      triangle is already how this window says a real problem
                      (a slot whose item is not equipped, a build the character
                      has drifted from). A dot says "active"; a triangle says
                      "wrong". They should not be the same glyph.

                      It follows the label rather than leading it. In front, it
                      pushed the words sideways the moment a control was set, so
                      the three captions stopped lining up with each other
                      exactly when one of them began to matter. --}}
                <div class="squire-build-token-field is-dimensions{{#unless tokenSettings.width.isDefault}} is-set{{/unless}}{{#unless tokenSettings.height.isDefault}} is-set{{/unless}}"
                     data-token-row="dimensions"
                     data-tooltip="How many grid spaces this token covers on the map.">
                    <span class="squire-build-token-label">
                        Dimensions
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-dot squire-build-token-change"
                           data-tooltip="<strong>On.</strong> Wearing this costume resizes the token to {{tokenSettings.width.value}} &times; {{tokenSettings.height.value}} grid space(s).<br>Click to switch it off, and the token keeps whatever size it already has."></i>
                    </span>
                    <div class="squire-build-token-control">
                        <input type="number" class="squire-build-token-input" data-token="width"
                               min="0.5" step="0.5" value="{{tokenSettings.width.value}}" aria-label="Token width">
                        <span class="squire-build-token-by">&times;</span>
                        <input type="number" class="squire-build-token-input" data-token="height"
                               min="0.5" step="0.5" value="{{tokenSettings.height.value}}" aria-label="Token height">
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="squire-build-token-field is-fit{{#unless tokenSettings.fit.isDefault}} is-set{{/unless}}"
                     data-token-row="fit"
                     data-tooltip="How the picture is fitted into the token's box.{{#each tokenSettings.fit.options}}<br><strong>{{this.label}}</strong> &mdash; {{this.help}}{{/each}}">
                    <span class="squire-build-token-label">
                        Image Fit
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-dot squire-build-token-change"
                           data-tooltip="<strong>On.</strong> Wearing this costume sets the image fit to {{tokenSettings.fit.label}}.<br>Click to switch it off, and the token keeps whatever fit it already has."></i>
                    </span>
                    <div class="squire-build-token-control">
                        <select class="squire-build-token-select" data-token="fit" aria-label="Image fit mode">
                            {{#each tokenSettings.fit.options}}
                            <option value="{{this.key}}"{{#if this.selected}} selected{{/if}}>{{this.label}}</option>
                            {{/each}}
                        </select>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="squire-build-token-field is-scale{{#unless tokenSettings.scale.isDefault}} is-set{{/unless}}"
                     data-token-row="scale"
                     data-tooltip="How large the picture is drawn inside that box.">
                    <span class="squire-build-token-label">
                        Scale
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-dot squire-build-token-change"
                           data-tooltip="<strong>On.</strong> Wearing this costume sets the token scale to {{tokenSettings.scale.value}}.<br>Click to switch it off, and the token keeps whatever scale it already has."></i>
                    </span>
                    <div class="squire-build-token-control">
                        <input type="range" class="squire-build-token-range" data-token="scale"
                               min="0.2" max="3" step="0.05" value="{{tokenSettings.scale.value}}" aria-label="Token scale">
                        <span class="squire-build-token-value">{{tokenSettings.scale.value}}</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

        <div class="squire-build-costume-main squire-build-image-slot{{#unless mainImage.isDefault}} is-set{{/unless}}"
             data-image="main"
             data-tooltip="{{#if mainImage.isDefault}}This costume has no picture of its own<br><em>Click to choose one</em>{{else}}Costume image<br><em>Click to change, right-click to reset</em>{{/if}}">
            <img src="{{mainImage.path}}" alt="{{build.name}}" data-image-kind="portrait">
        </div>

        {{!-- How the token is DRAWN, under the picture it is drawn with.

              A costume changes what a character looks like, and the artwork is
              only half of that: a giant in disguise is not the same size on the
              map, and a portrait cropped tall wants a different fit from one
              cropped square to sit right in the same box.

              Every control here can be UNSET, which is what "no change" means —
              it leaves the token exactly as it is, the same way an unset picture
              does. Right-click any of them to put it back to that. Applying a
              gear build never touches any of it. --}}

        </div>
    </div>
    {{/if}}
    {{#unless isCostume}}
    <div class="squire-build-doll">
        {{#if importReport}}
        {{!-- What the last import could not place, beside the doll rather than in a
              notification. These are things to DRAG ONTO THE FIGURE, so the list has
              to still be there while you drag — a toast that fades takes the names
              with it, and two permanent ones are a stack of warnings over the corner
              of the screen.

              Two reasons, kept apart because they have different answers. Nothing
              could say where it goes: a gap in what anything knows, and you fix it
              by putting it somewhere yourself. The slot was taken: not a failure at
              all — a character can equip two amulets on their sheet and has one
              neck. Rolled together the second reads as a bug in the first. --}}
        <div class="squire-build-report">
            <button type="button" class="squire-build-report-close" data-tooltip="Dismiss">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark"></i>
            </button>

            {{#if importReport.unknown.length}}
            <p><strong>Nowhere obvious to put {{#if (eq importReport.unknown.length 1)}}this{{else}}these{{/if}}:</strong>
               {{#each importReport.unknown}}{{#unless @first}}, {{/unless}}{{this}}{{/each}}</p>
            {{/if}}

            {{#if importReport.crowded.length}}
            <p><strong>No slot left for {{#if (eq importReport.crowded.length 1)}}this{{else}}these{{/if}}:</strong>
               {{#each importReport.crowded}}{{#unless @first}}, {{/unless}}{{this}}{{/each}}</p>
            {{/if}}

            <p class="squire-build-report-hint">Not in this build. Drag any of them onto the figure to add {{#if (eq importReport.unknown.length 1)}}it{{else}}them{{/if}}.</p>
        </div>
        {{/if}}

    <div class="squire-build-body">
        {{#each bodySlots}}
        <div class="squire-build-slot{{#if this.round}} is-round{{/if}}{{#if this.filled}} is-filled{{/if}}{{#if this.missing}} is-missing{{/if}}{{#if this.drifted}} is-drifted{{/if}}"
             data-rarity="{{this.rarity}}"
             style="grid-row: {{this.row}}; grid-column: {{this.column}};"
             data-slot="{{this.key}}"{{#if this.uuid}} data-item-uuid="{{this.uuid}}"{{/if}}
             data-tooltip="{{#if this.filled}}{{this.name}}{{#if this.drifted}}<br><strong>Not equipped</strong>{{/if}}<br><em>Right-click to clear</em>{{else if this.missing}}This item is no longer on the sheet<br><em>Right-click to clear</em>{{else}}<strong>{{this.label}}</strong>{{#if this.hint}}<br>{{this.hint}}{{/if}}<br><em>Drag one in from the Squire tray or your character sheet</em>{{/if}}">
            {{#if this.filled}}
            {{!-- Drawn like a favourites tile: the artwork IS the slot, with the
                  name over the bottom of it under a gradient. Same reasoning as
                  there — a caption panel becomes a band of colour across every
                  slot, and a text shadow vanishes on a pale icon. --}}
            <img class="squire-build-slot-image" src="{{this.img}}" alt="{{this.name}}">
            {{!-- The slot's own glyph, kept in the corner once the artwork has
                  covered the label. A full doll is otherwise sixteen pictures
                  with no way to tell which hole each one is filling. --}}
            <i class="fa-solid {{this.icon}} squire-build-slot-hint"></i>
            {{!-- This build is worn and this item is NOT on the character. The
                  slot keeps its picture — the plan still says this — and the
                  mark says the plan is not being met here. --}}
            {{#if this.drifted}}
            <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation squire-build-slot-drift"
               data-tooltip="{{this.name}} is not equipped, though this build is being worn"></i>
            {{/if}}
            {{!-- Attunement, as a gem in the corner. Lit when attuned, hollow and
                  warned when the item requires it and has not got it — the
                  second is the one worth seeing, because that item will do
                  nothing when the build is worn. --}}
            {{#if this.attuned}}
            <i class="fa-solid fa-gem squire-build-attunement is-attuned"></i>
            {{else if this.needsAttunement}}
            <i class="fa-regular fa-gem squire-build-attunement is-unattuned"></i>
            {{/if}}
            <span class="squire-build-slot-name">{{this.name}}</span>
            {{else if this.missing}}
            <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation squire-build-slot-icon is-warning"></i>
            <span class="squire-build-slot-label">{{this.label}}</span>
            {{else}}
            <i class="fa-solid {{this.icon}} squire-build-slot-icon"></i>
            <span class="squire-build-slot-label">{{this.label}}</span>
            {{/if}}
        </div>
        {{/each}}

        {{!-- Portrait and token, flanking the head. Not gear: these hold an image
              path, not an item, so they take a click rather than a drop. Round,
              like the ammo slots, because a circle marks "different kind of
              thing" without spending a word. --}}
        {{#each imageSlots}}
        <div class="squire-build-slot is-round squire-build-image-slot{{#unless this.isDefault}} is-set{{/unless}}"
             style="grid-row: {{this.row}}; grid-column: {{this.column}};"
             data-image="{{this.key}}"
             data-tooltip="{{this.label}}{{#if this.isDefault}} — this build does not change it, so the character's own stays<br><em>Click to choose an image</em>{{else}} — this build sets it when applied<br><em>Click to change, right-click to reset</em>{{/if}}">
            {{#if this.path}}
            <img class="squire-build-slot-image" src="{{this.path}}" alt="{{this.label}}" data-image-kind="{{this.key}}">
            {{/if}}
            <i class="fa-solid {{this.icon}} squire-build-slot-hint"></i>
            {{!-- An unset slot shows the character's CURRENT artwork, which made
                  it look chosen when it was not — and a build only writes the
                  images it actually sets, so an unset portrait silently changes
                  nothing on apply. The dashed border said that already; this
                  says it in a word. --}}
            {{#unless this.isDefault}}
            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-dot squire-build-image-change"
               data-tooltip="<strong>On.</strong> Wearing this sets the character's {{this.label}}.<br>Right-click the picture to switch it off, and the character keeps their own."></i>
            {{/unless}}
        </div>
        {{/each}}

        {{!-- The portrait, filling the middle of the doll. Not a slot and not
              droppable: it is there so the ring of slots reads as a body rather
              than as a scattered grid. --}}
        {{!-- The build's own picture. Browsed for like the portrait and the token,
              and unlike them it is never written to the character — a costume
              changes `actor.img`, and the centre of the doll is the one thing in
              this window that should hold still while the outfits change.
              Unset, it falls back through the build's portrait to the
              character's captured artwork. --}}
        <div class="squire-build-portrait squire-build-image-slot{{#unless mainImage.isDefault}} is-set{{/unless}}"
             style="grid-row: 2 / 5; grid-column: 2 / 5;"
             data-image="main"
             data-tooltip="{{#if mainImage.isDefault}}This build has no picture of its own<br><em>Click to choose one</em>{{else}}Build image<br><em>Click to change, right-click to reset</em>{{/if}}">
            <img src="{{mainImage.path}}" alt="{{actorName}}" data-image-kind="portrait">

            {{!-- The armour class, big, on the portrait's hem — where Baldur's
                  Gate puts it, and for the same reason: it is the number you are
                  actually playing against, and it belongs on the character
                  rather than in a line of footnotes.

                  It updates live while an item hovers a slot, which is why the
                  value and the delta are separate elements the window can write
                  to without re-rendering. --}}
            <div class="squire-build-ac-badge"
                 data-tooltip="Estimated from this build's armour, shield and Dexterity.<br>Class features, fighting styles and active effects are <strong>not</strong> counted, so this is for comparing builds rather than for your sheet.">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-shield squire-build-ac-badge-shield"></i>
                <span class="squire-build-ac-badge-value">{{armorClass.value}}</span>
                <span class="squire-build-ac-badge-label">AC</span>
                <span class="squire-build-ac-badge-delta" hidden></span>
            </div>

            {{!-- The totals, as plates on the portrait rather than a line of text
                  under everything. They describe the figure, so they belong on
                  it — and the armour class was already proving that the corners
                  of a portrait are the most readable place in this window. --}}
            <div class="squire-build-plate squire-build-plate-attunement{{#if attunement.over}} is-over{{/if}}"
                 data-tooltip="Attunement slots this build would use, out of what this character has.{{#if attunement.over}}<br><strong>This build needs more than they have.</strong>{{/if}}">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-gem"></i>
                <span>{{attunement.used}}/{{attunement.max}}</span>
            </div>

            <div class="squire-build-plate squire-build-plate-weight"
                 data-tooltip="What this build's gear weighs. Prepared spells are not counted, and a slotted stack counts once.">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-weight-hanging"></i>
                <span class="squire-build-weight-value">{{#if weight}}{{weight}}{{else}}0{{/if}}</span>
            </div>

            {{!-- What the character has on that this build never mentioned. There
              is no box on the doll for an item the plan does not name, so it is
              counted here rather than located. --}}
        {{#if drift}}
        <div class="squire-build-plate squire-build-plate-drift"
             data-tooltip="This build is being worn, but the character has drifted from it.{{#if drift.extraGear}}<br>{{drift.extraGear}} item{{#unless (eq drift.extraGear 1)}}s{{/unless}} equipped that this build does not include.{{/if}}{{#if drift.extraSpells}}<br>{{drift.extraSpells}} spell{{#unless (eq drift.extraSpells 1)}}s{{/unless}} prepared that this build does not include.{{/if}}<br><em>Equip the build again to put it back</em>">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-person-circle-exclamation"></i>
            <span>{{drift.count}}</span>
        </div>
        {{/if}}

        {{#if attunement.unattuned}}
            <div class="squire-build-plate squire-build-plate-warning"
                 data-tooltip="{{attunement.unattuned}} item{{#unless (eq attunement.unattuned 1)}}s{{/unless}} in this build require attunement and have not got it, so they would do nothing.">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i>
                <span>{{attunement.unattuned}}</span>
            </div>
            {{/if}}
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="squire-build-weapons">
        {{#each weaponSlots}}
        <div class="squire-build-slot{{#if this.filled}} is-filled{{/if}}{{#if this.missing}} is-missing{{/if}}{{#if this.drifted}} is-drifted{{/if}}"
             data-rarity="{{this.rarity}}"
             data-slot="{{this.key}}"{{#if this.uuid}} data-item-uuid="{{this.uuid}}"{{/if}}
             data-tooltip="{{#if this.filled}}{{this.name}}{{#if this.drifted}}<br><strong>Not equipped</strong>{{/if}}<br><em>Right-click to clear</em>{{else if this.missing}}This item is no longer on the sheet<br><em>Right-click to clear</em>{{else}}<strong>{{this.label}}</strong>{{#if this.hint}}<br>{{this.hint}}{{/if}}<br><em>Drag one in from the Squire tray or your character sheet</em>{{/if}}">
            {{#if this.filled}}
            {{!-- Drawn like a favourites tile: the artwork IS the slot, with the
                  name over the bottom of it under a gradient. Same reasoning as
                  there — a caption panel becomes a band of colour across every
                  slot, and a text shadow vanishes on a pale icon. --}}
            <img class="squire-build-slot-image" src="{{this.img}}" alt="{{this.name}}">
            {{!-- The slot's own glyph, kept in the corner once the artwork has
                  covered the label. A full doll is otherwise sixteen pictures
                  with no way to tell which hole each one is filling. --}}
            <i class="fa-solid {{this.icon}} squire-build-slot-hint"></i>
            {{!-- This build is worn and this item is NOT on the character. The
                  slot keeps its picture — the plan still says this — and the
                  mark says the plan is not being met here. --}}
            {{#if this.drifted}}
            <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation squire-build-slot-drift"
               data-tooltip="{{this.name}} is not equipped, though this build is being worn"></i>
            {{/if}}
            {{!-- Attunement, as a gem in the corner. Lit when attuned, hollow and
                  warned when the item requires it and has not got it — the
                  second is the one worth seeing, because that item will do
                  nothing when the build is worn. --}}
            {{#if this.attuned}}
            <i class="fa-solid fa-gem squire-build-attunement is-attuned"></i>
            {{else if this.needsAttunement}}
            <i class="fa-regular fa-gem squire-build-attunement is-unattuned"></i>
            {{/if}}
            <span class="squire-build-slot-name">{{this.name}}</span>
            {{else if this.missing}}
            <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation squire-build-slot-icon is-warning"></i>
            <span class="squire-build-slot-label">{{this.label}}</span>
            {{else}}
            <i class="fa-solid {{this.icon}} squire-build-slot-icon"></i>
            <span class="squire-build-slot-label">{{this.label}}</span>
            {{/if}}
        </div>
        {{/each}}
    </div>

    </div>

    {{#if isCaster}}
    {{!-- THE PREPARED COLUMN.

          Twenty-six cells, two across, down the side of the doll — and its size
          is not a choice. A cell is half a gear slot, so two of them stack into
          exactly one body row and the column keeps the doll's gridlines the
          whole way down; thirteen rows is what fits beside the body and the
          weapons under it.

          A caster's, and only a caster's. It briefly held carried potions for
          everybody else, which was the one thing in this window that applying
          could not enforce — there is no carried state in the system to set, so
          those cells looked exactly like the ones around them and did nothing.
          A martial's build is the doll, and their window is narrower by this
          column rather than padded out with it.

          Cells past the limit are dimmed and refuse drops: they are not empty,
          they are cells this character does not have YET, and drawing them is
          how the column says what levelling up will buy. --}}
    <div class="squire-build-pack">
        {{!-- The head of the column: exactly one body row tall, which is what
              drops the grid below it level with the top of the NECK slot rather
              than with the portrait circles above it. The spell slots live in
              that square, since it is the one place in the window they can go
              without pushing a cell out of true.

              A martial gets the same square holding nothing. It is not spare
              space, it is the offset — remove it and their column stops lining
              up with their doll. --}}
        <div class="squire-build-pack-head">
            {{#if spellSlots}}
            {{!-- The nine ranks as a three by three, reading left to right: 1st
                  in the corner, 9th in the far one. Position IS the label at
                  this size, and a grid of nine that never changes shape is
                  something you can read without counting. A rank the character
                  has not reached is dimmed and marked "--", the same statement
                  the dimmed cells below make.

                  A readout, never a drop target: in 5e you prepare a LIST and
                  cast any prepared spell with a slot of sufficient level, so
                  there is nothing to put in these. Once for the character, not
                  once per class, because a multiclass caster casts from one
                  pool. --}}
            <div class="squire-build-slot-ranks">
                {{#each spellSlots}}
                {{!-- A cell with a caption, not a bare figure: nine numbers in a
                      square told you nothing about which was which unless you
                      already knew the reading order. The caption is abbreviated
                      because the column is one gear slot wide and each of these
                      is a third of it — twenty-six pixels, which "Level 1" does
                      not fit in at a size anybody could read. The tooltip says
                      it in full. --}}
                <span class="squire-build-rank{{#unless this.has}} is-empty{{/unless}}"
                      data-tooltip="{{#if this.has}}<strong>Level {{this.label}}</strong><br>{{this.max}} slot{{#unless (eq this.max 1)}}s{{/unless}}, {{this.value}} still unspent{{else}}<strong>Level {{this.label}}</strong><br>No slots at this level yet{{/if}}">
                    <span class="squire-build-rank-label">Lvl {{this.level}}</span>
                    <span class="squire-build-rank-value">{{#if this.has}}{{this.max}}{{else}}&ndash;&ndash;{{/if}}</span>
                </span>
                {{/each}}
            </div>
            {{/if}}
        </div>

        <div class="squire-build-pack-grid">
            {{#each pack}}
            <div class="squire-build-pack-cell{{#if this.beyond}} is-beyond{{/if}}{{#if this.filled}} is-filled{{/if}}{{#if this.missing}} is-missing{{/if}}{{#if this.drifted}} is-drifted{{/if}}"
                 data-pack-index="{{this.index}}"{{#if this.uuid}} data-item-uuid="{{this.uuid}}"{{/if}}
                 data-tooltip="{{#if this.beyond}}<strong>Not yet</strong><br>This character cannot prepare this many spells at their level. The cell is here so you can see what levelling up will buy.{{else if this.filled}}{{this.name}}{{#if this.drifted}}<br><strong>Not prepared</strong>{{/if}}<br><em>Right-click to clear</em>{{else if this.missing}}This is no longer on the sheet<br><em>Right-click to clear</em>{{else}}<strong>Prepared spell</strong><br>Any levelled spell this character knows. Cantrips are always available and are not prepared, so they do not go here.<br><em>Drag one in from the Squire tray or your character sheet</em>{{/if}}">
                {{#if this.filled}}
                <img class="squire-build-slot-image" src="{{this.img}}" alt="{{this.name}}">
                {{#if this.drifted}}
                <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation squire-build-slot-drift"
                   data-tooltip="{{this.name}} is not prepared, though this build is being worn"></i>
                {{else if this.concentration}}
                <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-c squire-build-concentration" data-tooltip="Concentration"></i>
                {{/if}}
                {{!-- The spell's level, in the corner a gear slot uses for its
                      glyph: both answer "what kind of thing is this". --}}
                {{#if this.level}}
                <span class="squire-build-pack-mark">{{this.level}}</span>
                {{/if}}
                {{else if this.missing}}
                <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation squire-build-slot-icon is-warning"></i>
                {{else}}
                {{!-- The number, alone and centred. It shared the cell with a
                      sparkles glyph marking it as open, which two things then
                      fought over thirty-nine pixels — and the glyph was saying
                      what the cell's own dashed border and full brightness
                      already say next to a dimmed one. One mark, big enough to
                      read.

                      Numbered while empty and gone once filled: until there is a
                      picture in it a cell has nothing else to say for itself,
                      and "this is your eleventh of seventeen" is the context
                      that makes the column legible. Afterwards the spell is the
                      label and the number is noise. --}}
                <span class="squire-build-pack-number">{{this.position}}</span>
                {{/if}}
            </div>
            {{/each}}
        </div>
    </div>
    {{/if}}
    {{/unless}}

    </div>
    {{else}}
    {{!-- Nothing on the doll, for one of two reasons, and the page says which.

          It fills the window rather than collapsing it. A short panel was not
          only ugly: the rail beside it is a flex child that takes the height it
          is given, so a collapsed window squeezed the build list to nothing and
          the window claimed there was nothing to choose while holding a list of
          things to choose from.

          And it is the one screen anybody reads before they know what this
          window is, so it says what the two kinds of thing are. --}}
    <div class="squire-build-empty">
        <i class="fa-solid {{#if hasBuilds}}fa-hand-pointer{{else}}fa-shirt{{/if}} squire-build-empty-glyph"></i>

        {{#if hasBuilds}}
        <h3>Nothing selected</h3>
        <p>Choose a build or costume from the list on the left, or start another one.</p>
        {{else}}
        <h3>No builds yet</h3>
        <p>A place to plan what this character wears and carries, and to put it all on at once.</p>
        {{/if}}

        <dl class="squire-build-empty-kinds">
            <div>
                <dt><i class="fa-solid fa-shirt"></i> Build</dt>
                <dd>A set of gear. Drag items onto the figure to say what it is made of; equipping it
                    puts exactly those on and takes everything else off. It can plan prepared spells
                    too, if you switch that on.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
                <dt><i class="fa-solid fa-masks-theater"></i> Costume</dt>
                <dd>A portrait and a token, and how big that token is drawn. It changes only how the
                    character looks &mdash; never their gear or their spells.</dd>
            </div>
        </dl>

        <div class="squire-build-empty-actions">
            <button type="button" class="squire-build-rail-new" data-mode="gear"
                    data-tooltip="A set of gear to equip">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-shirt"></i> New Build
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="squire-build-rail-new" data-mode="costume"
                    data-tooltip="A portrait and token to wear. Changes how the character LOOKS and touches no gear.">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-masks-theater"></i> New Costume
            </button>
        </div>

        <p class="squire-build-empty-note">Nothing is applied to the character until you press the
            green button on a tile, and it asks first.</p>
    </div>
    {{/if}}

    </div>
</div>
